From 323a05a98a86c70fe565ebe6b788a593ffed93db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:42:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06908/11362] [outer-loop] ka59: round 7 no verified progress,
 lost to offline search churn

Round-7 gpt-5.6-sol session confirmed the banked L6 prefix, then chose
to trace the game's own Python source into an abstract state-space
model and ran an offline A* search rather than continuing direct live
exploration. The offline search succeeded (a 22-move plan found in
~97.5s), but the session then spent its remaining budget repeatedly
rewriting the translation/execution driver instead of settling on one
version and running it against the live env -- the same tooling-churn
failure mode as dc22's round 6, but rooted in over-investing in
offline simulation instead of live verification.

No new level was live-confirmed; the recovered 490-label candidate
sequence (prefix + 132-action tail) replays cleanly to level=6,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED, no win. No new level banked; frontier
stays at level 6. Next attempt should either continue round 6's
"what other launch source" live-exploration hypothesis directly, or
hard-budget the offline-search-to-live-execution handoff if retried.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
